  "notes": "じとじと describes an unpleasant damp or clammy feeling, often from sweat or humidity. It emphasizes the sticky, uncomfortable sensation more than just wetness.\n\nRELATED EXPRESSIONS:\n- むしむし: muggy (heat + humidity)\n- じめじめ: damp (environmental moisture)\n- べたべた: sticky (adhesive quality)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- じとじとする: to be damp/clammy\n- じとじとした{汗|あせ}: clammy sweat\n\nCOMPARISON:\n- じとじと emphasizes the uncomfortable clammy feeling\n- じめじめ emphasizes the dampness of an environment\n- Both are negative, but じとじと is more about personal discomfort",
